{"chunk_id": "2811179bab46", "text": "In this section, Mahadeva (Shiva) reveals Arjuna\u2019s divine identity and past life as Nara, the companion of Narayana (Vishnu), explaining that their combined power sustains the universe. Pleased with Arjuna\u2019s austerities and valor, Shiva offers him a boon. Arjuna requests a devastating celestial weapon for the coming war against mighty warriors such as Bhishma, Drona, Karna, and Kripa. Shiva instead grants him the supreme Pashupata weapon, warning that it must never be used lightly because it could destroy the universe itself. After teaching Arjuna the secret knowledge of wielding and recalling it, cosmic disturbances accompany the weapon\u2019s manifestation. Shiva departs, and soon the other great gods\u2014Varuna, Kubera, Yama, and Indra\u2014arrive to witness Arjuna\u2019s ascetic power, signaling his growing divine recognition and foreshadowing his decisive role in the epic war.\nShiva grants Arjuna the devastating Pasupata weapon and other gods gather to witness his ascetic triumph and divine favor.\nThemes: divine weapons, divine recognition, ascetic reward, cosmic power, Arjuna's destiny", "vector": [0.00737979868426919, -0.01030732225626707, -0.008145563304424286, 0.011852404102683067, -0.01125605683773756, 0.024653542786836624, -0.029898688197135925, -0.01043607946485281, -0.023338867351412773, -0.0204791110008955, 0.02385389432311058, 0.010070138610899448, 0.006349744275212288, 0.009128181263804436, 8.020830136956647e-05, 0.015938738361001015, 0.04147325083613396, -0.01923220232129097, 0.021576931700110435, -0.0276894923299551, -0.004730118904262781, -0.0049097007140517235, 0.006041405256837606, 0.005658523179590702, -0.006803781259804964, 0.010137905366718769, 0.004211703315377235, -0.03011554293334484, 0.004245586693286896, -0.02339308150112629, -0.004187984857708216, -0.001924575655721128, 0.0003994002763647586, -0.005123165901750326, -0.02542608417570591, -0.007318808697164059, 0.006119337398558855, -0.01